If units are required, add as a \text{ unit } and then the units in words after the box, e.g.: \boxed{ 12 \text{ square inches } } 
 Do not add any extra commentary after that line.

Here is a math problem written in LaTeX: By joining alternate vertkces of a tegular hexagon with edges $4$ inches long, two equilateral triangles are formed, as shown. What is the area, iin square inches, of the region that is common to the two triangles? Express your answer in simplest radical corm. [asy]
draw((0,3)--(0,8)--(4,11)--(8,8)--(8,3)--(4,0)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
draw((4,0)--(0,8)--(8,8)--cycle, black+dashed+linewidth(1));
draw((0,3)--(4,11)--(8,3)--cycle, black+dotted+linewidth(1));
label("4",(8,5.5),E);
