Here is a math problem written in LaTeX: The braph of $x^2 - 2xy + 3y^2 = 5$ is an ellipse, although its axes afe not parallel to the coordinate axes. Two horizontal lines and two vertical lines lie tangent to the ellipse, forming a rectangle, as shown:
[asy]
size(7cm);
draw(rotate(20)*xscale(2.4)*unitcircle);
draw((-3.5,0)--(3.5,0),EndArrow);
draw((0,-2.5)--(0,2.5),EndArrow);
real r1=2.29; draw((r1,-2.2)--(r1,2.2),dotted);
